Upstream-Name: PDrive for Linux
Upstream-Contact: Bertrand PRESLES <bpresles@gmail.com>
Source: https://github.com/bpresles/PDrive-for-Linux
Comment: Unofficial third-party client for Proton Drive, not affiliated with
 Proton AG. Third-party components are listed in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES
 (installed in /usr/share/doc/pdrive-for-linux/), as required by the MIT
 licence of the Proton components.

Files: *
Copyright: the PDrive for Linux authors
License: GPL-3+

Files: native/linux-x64/libproton_drive_sdk.so
Copyright: 2025-2026 Proton AG
License: Expat
Comment: Prebuilt (NativeAOT) from https://github.com/ProtonDriveApps/sdk at
 the revision recorded in native/linux-x64/SOURCES.txt. Licence text:
 LICENSE-proton-sdk.md. The library also embeds the .NET runtime (MIT, with
 its third-party notices: LICENSE-dotnet-runtime*.txt) and NuGet packages
 (MIT, BSD-3-Clause, Apache-2.0), see THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES and licenses/nuget-sdk.tsv.

Files: native/linux-x64/libproton_crypto.so
Copyright: 2025 Proton AG
License: Expat
Comment: Prebuilt from https://github.com/ProtonDriveApps/dotnet-crypto at the
 revision recorded in native/linux-x64/SOURCES.txt. Licence text:
 LICENSE-proton-dotnet-crypto.txt. Statically linked Rust crates (mostly MIT,
 also BSD-3-Clause, Apache-2.0, Zlib, Unicode-3.0, bzip2-1.0.6): see
 THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES and licenses/rust-proton-crypto.tsv.

Files: vendor/*
Copyright: the authors of each crate
License: other
Comment: Rust crates vendored with cargo vendor. Each directory carries its own
 licence files; THIRD_PARTY_CRATES.txt gives the licence expression declared by
 each crate. Audit of the crates linked into the programs (licenses/rust-pdrive.tsv):
 MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD-3-Clause, ISC, Zlib, Unicode-3.0, Unlicense, CDLA-Permissive-2.0,
 all compatible with GPL-3+.

